comments.body:
@CaroGo  
I only know the way of sideloading too. The play store support only official apks published over google.
The fossil gen 4 and gen 5 doesn't have usb, but you can activate debugging over wifi. Then you can use the ip address to connect directly from computer to watch by using abd-tool. Only remember that  same key for codesigning is required, otherwise the connect between watch and phone will be failed.

@Rig22  Iam really confused about this problem. On my Fossil 5 Gen, the play store don't show anythink from AAPS, so I install the wear.apk by abd through wifi-dev mode to my watch. Then all watchfaces are present in menu.

@MilosKozak was anythink changed in build process? The apk file is sized smaller then last stable.

--

The manual has more information to install wear.apk on your watch... See https://androidaps.readthedocs.io/en/latest/EN/Configuration/Watchfaces.html#building-wear-os-version-of-aaps

I hope this help anyone to deploy the watch-app, but the reasons for the problem is open and should be explained.
